1
00:00:16,676 --> 00:00:16,676
[Intro - metronome kick drum, one chiming delay guitar, a girl humming far away]

2
00:00:16,676 --> 00:00:16,676
[Verse 1 - male British voice, sing-spoken, close to the mic]

3
00:00:16,676 --> 00:00:22,660
Five in the morning, before the cockerel,

4
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:27,926
She's on the road with a yellow can.

5
00:00:27,926 --> 00:00:32,713
Red dust, bare feet, an hour each way,

6
00:00:32,713 --> 00:00:37,580
And it's heavier coming home.

7
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,612
She's seven. Same as my eldest.

8
00:00:40,612 --> 00:00:44,282
The water's brown. She drinks it anyway.

9
00:00:44,282 --> 00:00:46,755
Her brother coughs all night.

10
00:00:46,755 --> 00:00:49,468
She walks the long way round the school

11
00:00:49,468 --> 00:00:57,287
And doesn't go in.

12
00:00:57,287 --> 00:00:57,287
[Verse 2 - male, sing-spoken]

13
00:00:57,287 --> 00:01:00,479
Seven in the morning, green and pleasant land,

14
00:01:00,479 --> 00:01:04,229
The boiler hums, the tap runs hot,

15
00:01:04,229 --> 00:01:06,702
My boys are fighting over cereal

16
00:01:06,702 --> 00:01:10,293
And I'm moaning that the Wi-Fi's slow.

17
00:01:10,293 --> 00:01:13,085
Two pairs of school shoes by the door,

18
00:01:13,085 --> 00:01:16,516
Two lunchboxes, two coats, two futures,

19
00:01:16,516 --> 00:01:19,947
And her face came up on my phone again,

20
00:01:19,947 --> 00:01:24,734
And I scrolled on by.

21
00:01:24,734 --> 00:01:24,734
[Pre-Chorus - building, guitar climbing]

22
00:01:24,734 --> 00:01:28,085
Once, I said I'd do it later.

23
00:01:28,085 --> 00:01:31,436
Twice, I said what difference can one man make.

24
00:01:31,436 --> 00:01:35,745
Three times I scrolled on by,

25
00:01:35,745 --> 00:01:37,899
And somewhere a cockerel cried.

26
00:01:37,899 --> 00:01:37,899
[Chorus - soaring, full voice]

27
00:01:37,899 --> 00:01:42,207
Holy, holy,

28
00:01:42,207 --> 00:01:45,559
Wake me from my sleep.

29
00:01:45,559 --> 00:01:48,830
Every face that I scrolled past

30
00:01:48,830 --> 00:01:52,181
Was You, looking at me.

31
00:01:52,181 --> 00:01:52,181
(Will you sponsor me?)

32
00:01:52,181 --> 00:01:58,803
With the help of God, I will.

33
00:01:58,803 --> 00:01:58,803
(Will you sponsor me?)

34
00:01:58,803 --> 00:02:07,979
With the help of God, I will.

35
00:02:07,979 --> 00:02:07,979
[Verse 3 - male, warmer, the drums begin to move]

36
00:02:07,979 --> 00:02:11,330
A pound a day. A pound a day.

37
00:02:11,330 --> 00:02:14,521
Less than the coffee going cold beside me.

38
00:02:14,521 --> 00:02:17,394
It doesn't go in her pocket, it goes in the ground:

39
00:02:17,394 --> 00:02:20,266
A well, a nurse, a classroom roof,

40
00:02:20,266 --> 00:02:24,415
And four more children drinking there beside her.

41
00:02:24,415 --> 00:02:27,367
My son drew her a lion in felt-tip,

42
00:02:27,367 --> 00:02:29,681
Folded it into a padded envelope

43
00:02:29,681 --> 00:02:32,713
With stickers and a pack of crayons,

44
00:02:32,713 --> 00:02:36,223
And twelve weeks later, through the letterbox:

45
00:02:36,223 --> 00:02:42,048
A house, a blue door, and a sun with a face.

46
00:02:42,048 --> 00:02:42,048
[Spoken - soft young girl's voice, reading her letter]

47
00:02:42,048 --> 00:02:48,271
Dear friend. I am well. The water is clean now.

48
00:02:48,271 --> 00:02:52,021
I go to school. I am learning to write.

49
00:02:52,021 --> 00:02:54,814
I drew you my tree.

50
00:02:54,814 --> 00:02:54,814
[Chorus - soaring, full voice]

51
00:02:54,814 --> 00:02:58,085
Holy, holy,

52
00:02:58,085 --> 00:03:01,436
Wake me from my sleep.

53
00:03:01,436 --> 00:03:04,707
Every face that I scrolled past

54
00:03:04,707 --> 00:03:08,059
Was You, looking at me.

55
00:03:08,059 --> 00:03:08,059
(Will you sponsor me?)

56
00:03:08,059 --> 00:03:14,601
With the help of God, I will.

57
00:03:14,601 --> 00:03:14,601
(Will you sponsor me?)

58
00:03:14,601 --> 00:03:21,303
With the help of God, I will.

59
00:03:21,303 --> 00:03:21,303
[Bridge - building, drums driving, choir rising]

60
00:03:21,303 --> 00:03:24,734
You don't have to sing my song

61
00:03:24,734 --> 00:03:27,926
To know that this is wrong.

62
00:03:27,926 --> 00:03:32,234
You don't need my God to see a child

63
00:03:32,234 --> 00:03:35,346
Who's been waiting forty days.

64
00:03:35,346 --> 00:03:38,936
But I see a table long as the sky,

65
00:03:38,936 --> 00:03:42,447
Laid on a mountain in the light,

66
00:03:42,447 --> 00:03:46,037
Every nation, every tribe and tongue,

67
00:03:46,037 --> 00:03:49,309
No colour, no border, no first, no last,

68
00:03:49,309 --> 00:03:53,777
And a chair beside her with your name on.

69
00:03:53,777 --> 00:03:57,048
Let the little children come.

70
00:03:57,048 --> 00:04:03,750
Let the little children come.

71
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:08,138
Whoever welcomes one of these

72
00:04:08,138 --> 00:04:13,484
Welcomes Me.

73
00:04:13,484 --> 00:04:13,484
[Final Chorus - key lift, full band, the whole congregation]

74
00:04:13,484 --> 00:04:16,676
Holy, holy,

75
00:04:16,676 --> 00:04:19,947
Wake us from our sleep.

76
00:04:19,947 --> 00:04:23,218
Every face that we scrolled past

77
00:04:23,218 --> 00:04:25,293
Was You, looking at us.

78
